            "content": "<!-- qualor:issue e50aa582-2292-4a12-830a-fa6e00002c63 -->\n**AI review** · High · Logic · likely · ` ai:logic `\n\n**canDeleteAccount grants deletion to non-admins, contradicting its documented rule**\n\nThe doc comment says only administrators may delete accounts, but ` !user.isAdmin ` returns true for every non-admin and false for admins, so the check is inverted. Any caller that uses it for authorization would let ordinary users delete accounts and refuse administrators. The expression also throws a TypeError when ` user ` is null or undefined. Return the admin check directly and guard the null case, as in the suggestion.\n\n```suggestion\nexport const canDeleteAccount = (user) => user?.isAdmin === true;\n```\n\n[View in Qualor](https://ado.example.invalid/projects/8d5b4ae3-0139-44f7-8246-fa6e000000b8/issues/e50aa582-2292-4a12-830a-fa6e00002c63)",
