            "content": "<!-- qualor:issue f66e84be-da61-4b0a-8d3b-fa6e00000a80 -->\n**AI review** · Medium · Tests · possible · ` ai:tests `\n\n**New authorization rule canDeleteAccount has no test, so an inverted or removed check goes unnoticed**\n\ncanDeleteAccount is a new access-control predicate. A grep finds no reference to it anywhere in the repository, so no test pins the admin-only behaviour. Changing ` !user.isAdmin ` to ` user.isAdmin `, or dropping the check, would pass unnoticed. Add a unit test asserting true for an admin and false for a non-admin, and cover a missing or undefined ` isAdmin `.\n\nAssumes: The repository normally tests modules like this one, and the function is meant to be called from application code.\n\n[View in Qualor](https://ado.example.invalid/projects/8d5b4ae3-0139-44f7-8246-fa6e000000b8/issues/f66e84be-da61-4b0a-8d3b-fa6e00000a80)",
